WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:04.250
<b>KEIO YEAR 3 (1867)</b>

00:05.670 --> 00:07.080
Long time no see.

00:07.290 --> 00:08.830
How's life been treatin' ya?

00:09.460 --> 00:11.170
What are you doing here?

00:11.170 --> 00:15.250
Yeesh, not much of a welcome.
You got beef with me or what?

00:16.210 --> 00:17.880
I wouldn't put it that way.

00:19.710 --> 00:22.710
Well, I'm here to treat you to a cup o' tea.

00:23.210 --> 00:25.540
You came all the way from Kyoto for that?

00:25.540 --> 00:26.670
Yup.

00:26.670 --> 00:29.630
Anyhoo, you'll let me in, won'tcha?

00:32.920 --> 00:36.670
I gotta say, your digs are as bland as ever.

00:42.880 --> 00:45.000
Gone from hunter to kidnapper, eh?

00:45.500 --> 00:47.000
That's my daughter.

00:47.000 --> 00:47.750
Huh?!

00:48.960 --> 00:51.040
Your daughter, really?

00:52.210 --> 00:54.830
Hi there, lil' missy. What's your name?

01:00.290 --> 01:01.380
Nomari.

01:03.460 --> 01:08.330
Sorry if I spooked ya, Nomari-chan.
But I got some business with your daddy here.

01:11.960 --> 01:14.830
Such good manners. Hard to believe that you raised her.

01:15.290 --> 01:16.130
Right?

01:17.830 --> 01:20.710
Shucks, I wasn't expecting ya to just agree with me!

02:57.830 --> 02:58.670
What's this?

02:59.130 --> 03:01.920
A natsume tea caddy. Well-crafted, ain't it?

03:02.790 --> 03:05.460
Except that nobody seems to care for it.

03:06.080 --> 03:08.670
So it's just been sittin' and gathering dust.

03:09.420 --> 03:10.960
It's the hydrangeas, I'd bet.

03:11.330 --> 03:12.000
Hm?

03:12.630 --> 03:16.130
Hydrangeas can change color
based on the soil they're grown in.

03:17.080 --> 03:22.420
Therefore, many people consider these flowers to be
a bad omen that represents treachery and fickleness.

03:22.830 --> 03:24.920
Oh? Go figure!

03:25.290 --> 03:27.000
Or so I was once told.

03:27.170 --> 03:29.210
Still, this is a solid piece of work.

03:29.210 --> 03:31.290
It'd be a shame to just let it go to waste.

03:31.500 --> 03:35.580
So here I am, hopin' that you'd be willing to use it
to make us some tasty cups o' tea.

03:37.500 --> 03:39.170
You think I know how to make tea?

03:39.170 --> 03:41.880
Well, shoot. That's my bad!

03:42.290 --> 03:46.920
I ain't cultured enough to know the first thing
about how to perform a proper tea ceremony, myself.

03:50.500 --> 03:53.420
I don't suppose ya know anybody that could?

03:54.170 --> 03:56.540
Well, there is one person who comes to mind...

03:57.040 --> 03:58.580
Oh, that's great!

03:59.000 --> 04:02.460
Then let's go. We can all chew the fat over some tea.

04:03.540 --> 04:06.880
Then catch up on ghost and demon news, too.

04:11.880 --> 04:14.170
Wow, look at how big this sweet pea has gotten!

04:14.330 --> 04:18.710
Oh, stop it. You saw her just the other day, Dad.

04:18.710 --> 04:19.420
Huh?

04:19.670 --> 04:23.420
Well, yeah. But kids grow extra fast
whenever you're not looking.

04:23.420 --> 04:26.790
Like by a head or two every day!

04:27.250 --> 04:31.830
Trust me, Ofuu. I still remember the days
when you were all teensy-weeny!

04:33.170 --> 04:34.460
Enough, Dad.

04:35.670 --> 04:38.830
Oh! I should hurry and make her a cup of tea.

04:39.330 --> 04:42.920
Gosh. Looks like Nomari-chan's
already stealing hearts, eh?

04:43.080 --> 04:46.920
Yep. Although, I think it's more
that my dad is just a lovesick puppy.

04:49.710 --> 04:51.710
Ofuu. Will you watch her?

04:51.710 --> 04:52.380
Sure.

04:52.920 --> 04:55.290
Have a good time, Daddy.

05:00.540 --> 05:02.170
Have fun!

05:08.170 --> 05:09.250
See you later.

05:12.670 --> 05:17.460
Just putting it out there, but I bet that soba chef
knew how to perform a tea ceremony, no?

05:23.580 --> 05:24.750
Maybe so.

05:27.040 --> 05:29.500
Well, life's complicated.

05:29.880 --> 05:33.040
Both people and towns...

05:33.670 --> 05:36.380
something's always different whenever you see them.

05:36.580 --> 05:39.580
They change in the blink of an eye,
even if you never notice.

05:41.040 --> 05:44.130
And if that's making ya feel a little lonesome, well...

05:45.540 --> 05:47.630
maybe it's just a sign you're getting old?

05:48.460 --> 05:49.500
Hell if I know.

05:50.630 --> 05:53.080
Jeez. You sure ya don't got beef with me?

05:54.580 --> 05:57.790
Oh, hey! Wanna do some hanami?

05:57.790 --> 06:00.960
Your friend who can help us
make tea lives this way, right?

06:00.960 --> 06:03.080
I know a spot along the way.

06:03.880 --> 06:06.460
Hanami? You mean look at cherry blossoms?

06:06.540 --> 06:07.380
Yup!

06:07.630 --> 06:08.880
But they're not in season.

06:09.130 --> 06:11.000
Oh, pshaw.

06:13.500 --> 06:18.290
Whaddya think? Pretty classy looking shop, eh?

06:46.170 --> 06:47.790
Where are the cherry blossoms?

06:47.920 --> 06:49.040
Don't fret.

06:50.040 --> 06:52.830
Nice. This is good stuff.

06:55.130 --> 06:57.080
Ya look confused.

06:57.670 --> 07:00.830
C'mere. Feast your eyes on this one.

07:03.630 --> 07:05.290
This is bizen ware.

07:05.630 --> 07:09.420
It's made with only clay and fire. No glaze whatsoever.

07:09.420 --> 07:11.000
Looks pretty rustic, eh?

07:11.500 --> 07:15.920
But these cups are great for sake cuz they enhance
the aroma and make it taste extra smooth.

07:16.420 --> 07:18.330
That's fascinating.

07:18.580 --> 07:22.170
Hah, I knew that'd get your attention!

07:23.960 --> 07:25.290
Over here is kutani ware.

07:26.250 --> 07:28.880
The lavish aesthetics are their big selling point.

07:29.630 --> 07:31.580
Flowers, birds, landscapes...

07:31.880 --> 07:36.380
They're just as much beautiful paintings
as they are dishware.

07:39.670 --> 07:44.750
It was actually a goldsmith who founded kutani ware,
so it shares a bond with the Akitsu style.

07:50.540 --> 07:53.210
Well? Pretty interesting stuff, huh?

07:54.580 --> 07:57.580
Learning the history behind these
makes me see them in a new light.

07:57.750 --> 07:59.920
Glad to hear it!

07:59.920 --> 08:02.330
But ya gotta be careful.

08:02.830 --> 08:07.580
These can turn people into connoisseurs who take on
enough debt to ruin their lives over a single plate.

08:08.040 --> 08:11.330
I'd never get in that deep. I have a daughter to care for.

08:12.080 --> 08:13.830
Hope that stays true!

08:24.380 --> 08:26.750
This is what I came here for.

08:30.080 --> 08:33.960
Nabeshima ware. A plate decorated with enamel
cherry blossoms and a brushwood fence.

08:34.460 --> 08:36.250
A real beaut, ain't it?

08:36.790 --> 08:39.460
You're right. This is a good spot for hanami.

08:39.880 --> 08:44.790
Every piece here is filled with the hopes and dreams
of the craftsman who made it.

08:47.580 --> 08:51.000
And the best part? These flowers never go out of season.

08:51.580 --> 08:53.710
They've been the same since 100 years ago.

08:53.710 --> 08:55.960
And'll stay the same for 100 more.

09:01.420 --> 09:04.420
Shucks! Beggin' your pardon, good sir.

09:04.880 --> 09:07.380
Sorry to bug ya with my silly request.

09:07.920 --> 09:10.830
Akitsu-dono, was it? That's okay.

09:10.830 --> 09:14.170
Tea ceremonies are not exactly my forte,
but I know how they're done.

09:14.580 --> 09:18.170
Besides, I enjoy partaking in
a leisurely cup of tea from time to time.

09:18.670 --> 09:22.420
My apologies. Neither of us
have experience with tea ceremonies.

09:22.580 --> 09:24.130
I hope you'll forgive any mistakes we make.

09:24.710 --> 09:28.830
Nitpicking over proper etiquette
runs counter to the primary essence of tea.

09:29.210 --> 09:32.710
Please, don't be so tense. Just enjoy yourselves.

09:34.830 --> 09:37.330
Okay. Please wait a moment.

10:01.000 --> 10:01.880
Here you are.

10:11.540 --> 10:12.750
Delicious.

10:13.500 --> 10:15.080
I'm glad you think so.

10:18.290 --> 10:20.580
Aren't we supposed to drink from the same cup in turn?

10:20.750 --> 10:23.080
That's one way of doing it.

10:23.330 --> 10:27.670
But in the interest of socializing, I thought it best
to prepare a separate cup for each of us.

10:28.330 --> 10:30.290
Here. Please enjoy, Akitsu-dono.

10:30.790 --> 10:31.830
Thank ya kindly.

10:32.290 --> 10:35.630
I must say, I'm really struck by your generosity, good sir.

10:36.500 --> 10:41.500
Oh, think nothing of it. I gladly consider
any friend of Jin-dono's as a friend of mine.

10:41.880 --> 10:45.210
Make yourself at home.
I don't even mind if you sit cross-legged.

10:46.540 --> 10:49.210
Shucks, I don't wanna be that audacious!

10:52.210 --> 10:53.580
Mmm! Tasty!

11:08.500 --> 11:09.460
Long way down.

11:09.460 --> 11:12.670
Ready? Three, two, one... go!

11:18.330 --> 11:20.130
Come on down, Jinta!

11:20.630 --> 11:22.000
O-okay!

11:35.040 --> 11:37.210
Hey, that actually felt pretty good!

11:37.210 --> 11:38.460
I know, right?

11:38.750 --> 11:40.710
It's your turn next, you two!

11:42.420 --> 11:43.420
Suzune-chan!

11:45.080 --> 11:45.670
Let's go!

11:45.670 --> 11:46.960
S-sure...

11:46.960 --> 11:48.130
We'll do it together.

11:48.630 --> 11:50.250
Three, two, one, go!

11:52.330 --> 11:54.420
Isn't this fun, Suzune-chan?

11:54.830 --> 11:55.750
Yeah!

12:01.710 --> 12:03.500
Congrats on your first jump, Suzune-chan!

12:06.250 --> 12:07.210
I wanna go again.

12:08.750 --> 12:10.210
Sure! Let's go!

12:10.210 --> 12:10.920
Me, too!

12:10.920 --> 12:12.210
Me three!

12:12.210 --> 12:13.710
C'mon, everybody!

12:18.040 --> 12:22.380
Ya know, I reckon the tea tastes
even better thanks to this caddy.

12:22.380 --> 12:24.540
Indeed. It's a beautiful piece.

12:24.790 --> 12:26.500
You've got great taste!

12:26.500 --> 12:29.210
This here's actually the work
of a fairly distinguished craftsman.

12:29.790 --> 12:30.710
Wow!

12:31.460 --> 12:33.290
Is something the matter, Jin-dono?

12:35.210 --> 12:35.880
No.

12:37.080 --> 12:40.250
Though I'd argue that calling Somegoro
my "friend" is a bit of a stretch.

12:41.630 --> 12:43.880
Yeesh. You're always so mean to me.

12:44.210 --> 12:47.710
But I reckon it's hard for anybody to be
as chummy as the two of you seem to be!

12:48.040 --> 12:50.330
I'm happy that's the impression you get.

12:50.630 --> 12:54.000
He's a good friend who I've known longer than any other.

12:54.710 --> 13:00.580
Oh? That's funny, cuz this yokel ain't near prestigious
enough to earn that kinda praise. Trust me!

13:01.170 --> 13:06.080
Social status makes no difference. Though, I realize
it's unfair for a samurai like me to claim that.

13:06.460 --> 13:11.000
But even so, I cherish the bond
that I've forged with Jin-dono.

13:11.580 --> 13:15.830
And hopefully, we can maintain it
for many years to come.

13:31.170 --> 13:33.420
Chitose-chan, look at these!

13:40.750 --> 13:42.500
Wow! How pretty!

13:49.250 --> 13:51.670
What's the matter, Chitose-chan?

13:53.000 --> 13:55.040
Oh, it's nothing.

13:55.790 --> 13:56.630
Shall we go?

13:56.880 --> 13:57.880
All right.

14:00.580 --> 14:03.920
Really? Well, we should go together next time!

14:03.920 --> 14:04.540
Sure!

14:17.790 --> 14:21.580
You're right. Hopefully, we'll stay close.

14:22.750 --> 14:25.040
Yes. Indeed.

14:41.420 --> 14:44.380
Akitsu-dono. I understand you hail from Kyoto.

14:45.210 --> 14:46.380
I sure do.

14:47.540 --> 14:49.750
How are things going lately?

14:50.290 --> 14:51.080
In Kyoto?

14:51.880 --> 14:53.040
Let me think.

14:54.540 --> 14:58.290
Well, we've had a feisty bunch of visitors
comin' from Satsuma, Choshu, and the like.

14:58.290 --> 15:00.580
Things are kind of a mess!

15:04.420 --> 15:08.830
Beggin' your pardon.
Did my answer rub ya the wrong way?

15:09.670 --> 15:11.130
Oh, not at all.

15:16.630 --> 15:20.080
Shucks, that was tasty. I'm mighty grateful!

15:21.170 --> 15:22.290
Same here.

15:22.750 --> 15:25.710
Getting to relax in such good company
was a rare treat for me.

15:26.750 --> 15:27.460
Toodle-oo!

15:29.380 --> 15:30.210
Jin-dono.

15:33.380 --> 15:36.880
If you don't mind, could we spar sometime soon?

15:37.880 --> 15:39.460
Why the sudden interest?

15:40.080 --> 15:43.290
No reason. Just want to get some exercise.

15:43.920 --> 15:45.420
I'll gladly spar with you.

15:46.290 --> 15:48.250
But don't hesitate to ask if you need help with something.

15:52.960 --> 15:53.710
Right.

15:54.000 --> 15:56.210
I will. When the time comes.

16:03.710 --> 16:06.130
You're lucky to have him as a friend.

16:06.380 --> 16:07.420
I suppose.

16:08.170 --> 16:10.920
So, what did you really come here for?

16:10.920 --> 16:13.540
Exactly what I told ya before, silly.

16:13.540 --> 16:15.830
Just wanted to chat and have some tea.

16:16.460 --> 16:18.380
And we finished all that.

16:18.750 --> 16:21.000
Now it's time to talk demons.

16:23.130 --> 16:27.460
Like I told your samurai friend,
things have been getting dicey.

16:28.210 --> 16:32.170
Demons are poppin' up like mushrooms, even in Kyoto.

16:32.880 --> 16:36.500
And now, a nasty rumor's been going 'round
the exorcist community.

16:37.130 --> 16:39.130
It's weird how they keep proliferating,

16:39.130 --> 16:42.880
so people believe there's some kinda
demonic kingpin in control.

16:44.790 --> 16:46.000
Somegoro Akitsu.

16:46.330 --> 16:49.710
Has anybody described this kingpin?
Like maybe their hair color?

16:50.000 --> 16:53.630
Nah. Nobody's actually seen 'em in person.

16:53.880 --> 16:57.670
Could be a hulking monster or some kinda she-devil...

17:03.670 --> 17:05.540
Can't be sure yet.

17:08.130 --> 17:10.040
So, whatcha gonna do?

17:10.330 --> 17:11.790
Good question.

17:16.420 --> 17:20.630
Well, it's only a rumor. Ain't no proof yet.

17:20.880 --> 17:23.710
But ya better keep that nugget in the back of your mind.

17:24.130 --> 17:26.830
Duly noted. Sorry for all the hassle.

17:27.000 --> 17:29.830
Aw, it's fine. Just a simple "thanks" will do!

17:29.960 --> 17:32.080
I really did want to have tea with ya.

17:32.080 --> 17:36.580
And we covered the demon news.
Plus, I even took care of my little ghost problem.

17:37.290 --> 17:39.540
I'd call that a satisfying day!

17:41.250 --> 17:42.790
Well, toodle-oo!

17:44.710 --> 17:46.000
Somegoro Akitsu.

17:46.710 --> 17:52.380
We're done with tea and demons.
But I've yet to hear about this "ghost" problem.

17:53.040 --> 17:55.750
Like I said, it's all taken care of!

18:00.580 --> 18:04.040
I was plannin' to send it off by myself, but...

18:04.920 --> 18:08.710
This natsume here was shunned
not just for the hydrangea design,

18:08.710 --> 18:11.540
but also cuz strange phenomena occur in its presence.

18:11.540 --> 18:13.540
It got passed 'round like a rotten potato.

18:14.380 --> 18:18.750
Until, finally, it's last owner passed away.

18:18.750 --> 18:24.380
Nobody ever used it in its lifetime.
Then it got left to rot in an abandoned house.

18:25.330 --> 18:29.750
The poor thing. I mean, just look at how adorable it is.

18:30.920 --> 18:33.250
Okay, but what about the ghost?

18:33.630 --> 18:37.040
The emotions infused in this tea caddy brought it to life.

18:37.460 --> 18:39.710
As an Akitsu, I couldn't just toss it out.

18:39.710 --> 18:42.250
So I brought it along to give it a proper goodbye.

18:43.040 --> 18:45.710
It was mighty interested in you, by the way.

18:46.040 --> 18:48.500
Enjoyed its first time doing hanami, too.

18:49.250 --> 18:54.210
It also loved seeing all the different porcelain
and pottery displayed in that shop.

18:57.040 --> 18:59.130
A truly fulfilling day.

19:16.420 --> 19:19.790
The tsumogami shaman who can turn
the emotions of objects into demons.

19:20.630 --> 19:23.250
This method of exorcism is unique to you, I suppose.

19:26.210 --> 19:29.420
Swinging a flashy blade around
isn't the only way to dispel spirits, ya know.

19:29.790 --> 19:32.960
Sometimes the key to making them move on
is to befriend them.

19:33.380 --> 19:37.000
That's rich coming from a guy who just attacked me
without even trying to talk it out.

19:37.000 --> 19:38.790
Different strokes!

19:41.080 --> 19:43.380
Alrighty. Goodbye for real.

19:43.960 --> 19:48.420
Maybe next time we can have
sake over tea, eh? At my place!

20:04.290 --> 20:07.080
Nomari-chan was well behaved while you were away.

20:07.080 --> 20:08.210
That's good.

20:08.210 --> 20:10.460
Hey, sweet pea. How's it taste?

20:11.420 --> 20:13.210
Um, it's plain.

20:13.580 --> 20:17.630
Yep. There's no doubt that she's your kid, pal!

20:23.500 --> 20:24.330
Nomari.

20:29.960 --> 20:33.210
Who'd a thunk the big bad demon hunter
was such a doting dad!

20:33.210 --> 20:34.500
Say what you will.

20:35.040 --> 20:38.170
Well, I sure as heck ain't one to talk.

20:40.040 --> 20:41.580
Thanks for da food!

20:42.250 --> 20:43.580
Nicely done.

20:49.380 --> 20:50.580
Daddy!

20:51.330 --> 20:52.380
What's gotten into you?

21:00.210 --> 21:04.420
Whaddya say, pal?
Nothing quite like having a daughter, eh?

21:05.460 --> 21:06.130
Yeah.

21:07.210 --> 21:11.000
Fathers can't help but fret over their kids. I get that now.

21:12.330 --> 21:16.460
By the way, have you considered
that she might need a mother figure, too?

21:16.880 --> 21:19.130
I got the perfect candidate. You can have my Ofuu.

21:19.460 --> 21:20.750
Come off it, Dad!

21:20.830 --> 21:22.540
But I'm serious, Ofuu.

21:22.750 --> 21:24.540
We can talk about this later.

21:24.920 --> 21:29.170
You haven't been in the best shape lately.
Why not call it quits early and get some rest?

21:29.790 --> 21:32.210
Oh, worried about little ol' me?

21:32.630 --> 21:36.540
It's more that I can't clean the table off
if you just sit there forever.

21:37.000 --> 21:41.460
Ouch. Feels like Ofuu's been
on a real mean streak lately.

21:42.460 --> 21:47.210
Will a day come when Nomari
starts treating me like that, too?

21:50.290 --> 21:53.290
Gosh, it's a little early to be worried about that.

21:53.750 --> 21:56.290
Oh, Jinya-kun. You've really changed!

21:57.420 --> 21:58.710
Have I?

22:01.920 --> 22:02.920
I see.

22:04.080 --> 22:06.420
I'm glad it seems that way.
